If this is a default compile of NetHack, you probably have to do
something like:

chgrp -R games /usr/games/lib/nethackdir
chmod -R g+w /usr/games/lib/nethackdir
chmod g+s /usr/games/lib/nethackdir/nethack

assuming your have a "games" group (you could create a new
"games" group in /etc/group if you don't already have one).

If that doesn't work, well, heck if I know what you need to do; perhaps
you could describe which files and directories were in the package you
installed?

I build NetHack from source myself, with the
VAR_PLAYGROUND="/var/games/nethack" option, and make /var/games/nethack
and the files under it have group owner group "games" and
.../nethackdir/nethack setgid to "games" ("chmod g+s
.../nethackdir/nethack", where "..." is the location of nethackdir,
usually /usr/games/lib or /usr/local/lib).  The old defaults where
NetHack wants to write to files under /usr/games/lib/nethackdir is just
not the right thing to do any more.  Making NetHack setuid, unless it's
to a unique user, is probably not a great idea either (and especially
don't make it setuid to root).

